{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-2m5v-pch6-74hx","cve_id":"CVE-2026-109383","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-2m5v-pch6-74hx","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2m5v-pch6-74hx","summary":"undici vulnerable to TLS certificate validation bypass via dropped tls options in Agent","description":"### Impact\n\nundici's `Agent` passes its constructor options through a JSON-based deep clone (`JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(...))`) before forwarding them to each per-origin `Pool`. JSON cannot represent functions, so a caller-supplied `tls` option containing a `checkServerIdentity` callback is silently dropped before it reaches the TLS layer. As a result, a TLS peer whose certificate a custom `checkServerIdentity` was written to reject, but which passes Node's default hostname and chain checks, is silently accepted when the request is made through `Agent`. Because `Agent` is the default dispatcher behind `request`, `fetch`, and `setGlobalDispatcher`, this is the path most applications use. `EnvHttpProxyAgent` is also affected on its direct and `NO_PROXY` routes, which delegate to an internal `Agent`.\n\nOnly applications that pass a function-valued `tls` option (such as a custom `checkServerIdentity` for certificate or public-key pinning) are affected. Passing the same options through `connect` is not affected. This is the `Agent` counterpart of the `BalancedPool` certificate validation bypass fixed in CVE-2026-84961.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to undici `6.29.1`, `7.30.1`, or `8.12.2`. `Agent` now preserves the `tls` option outside the JSON clone, so custom TLS verification callbacks are forwarded to each origin unchanged.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nPass the TLS options through `connect` instead of `tls`. For proxied `EnvHttpProxyAgent` destinations, use `requestTls` / `proxyTls`.","type":"reviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nodejs/undici/security-advisories/GHSA-2m5v-pch6-74hx","source_code_location":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-2m5v-pch6-74hx","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-109383","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-2m5v-pch6-74hx","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-109383","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/04cb74b1db131ff8f5b4557dce811cbf5f4664b4","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/8c59f6b302898cb2e9b0f7962cd7212b6e597c9f","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/f75eac00ac177f7b2e6c8bfbd52d4113164286e6","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v6.29.1","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v7.30.1","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v8.12.2","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2m5v-pch6-74hx"],"published_at":"2026-10-27T19:02:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T19:02:27Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-10-27T19:02:26Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-10-15T19:17:20Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 4.0.0, < 6.29.1","first_patched_version":"6.29.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 7.0.0, < 7.30.1","first_patched_version":"7.30.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 8.0.0, < 8.12.2","first_patched_version":"8.12.2","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N","score":7.4},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-295","name":"Improper Certificate Validation"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"euriconicacio","id":5957301,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NTczMDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5957301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/euriconicacio","html_url":"https://github.com/euriconicacio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/euriconicacio/followers",